codex
The existing layered-chain draft does not survive the required oracle loop: easy and medium were solved, and the hard rung was also solved in two of three calls. Its polynomial route cost only 3,361 edge scans—far too close to the 240-operation “shortcut”—so it fails H even on Track B.

I’m retiring that family and replacing it with a different native KEP family: a full cycle packing in a layered compatibility graph, represented exactly by affine maps over a finite field. The planted cycle factor will be a short symbolic witness; generic meet-in-the-middle composition costs millions of modular operations, while the construction’s shared fixed-point invariant takes under 300.
