The replacement module now generates the certificate strictly by composition: the selected affine maps share one global fixed point and their slopes multiply to 1, so they expand to a full set of disjoint KEP cycles. The answer is a short symbolic map word (10 records), while the graph itself has 100,070 vertices at the hard preset but is represented exactly and compactly. I’m running the full gates now, including the million-operation reference search and relabelling proofs.
