codex
Outcome: **parked as `cap_bound`; not shipped or rejected**.

I verified the paper’s native KEP definition and algorithms: Section 1 defines feasible path/cycle packings, while Theorems 1–3 provide exponential deterministic and randomized algorithms, requiring an honest Track B classification. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.18471v2)

Implemented artifacts:

- [gen_2603_18471.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/gen_2603_18471.py) — deterministic affine cycle-factor generator and exact verifier
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/.meta.json)
- [rejected_gen_2603_18471.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.18471/rejected_gen_2603_18471.py) — retained earlier, easier chain-family attempt

Key measurements:

- All G1–G9(c) local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Reference search: 1,365,236 finite-field operations.
- Compact route: 259 operations.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Answer: 399 characters, 30 atomic values.
- Oracle loop: easy, medium, hard, and escalated levels were each solved 3/3.

Following the contract, hinted/placebo runs were not performed after `cap_bound`, and no `REJECTED.md` was created.
